# Python IDEs

An IDE (Integrated Development Environment) helps write, run, and debug code efficiently.

---

## VS Code

Visual Studio Code is the most popular Python editor.

### Features

* Lightweight
* Fast
* Extensions Support
* Git Integration
* Debugging Tools

### Installation

1. Download VS Code.
2. Install Python Extension.
3. Create a Python file.
4. Run the code.

---

## PyCharm

PyCharm is a professional Python IDE.

### Features

* Intelligent Code Completion
* Built-in Debugger
* Refactoring Tools
* Project Management

### Editions

* Community Edition (Free)
* Professional Edition (Paid)

---

# VS Code vs PyCharm

| Feature                  | VS Code         | PyCharm           |
| ------------------------ | --------------- | ----------------- |
| Free                     | Yes             | Community Edition |
| Speed                    | Fast            | Moderate          |
| Extensions               | Large Ecosystem | Built-In Features |
| Beginner Friendly        | Yes             | Yes               |
| Professional Development | Good            | Excellent         |

